{"task_id": "HumanEval/29", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef filter_by_prefix(strings: List[str], prefix: str) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Filters an input list of strings, returning only those that start with the given prefix.\n\n    The comparison is case-sensitive. The order of elements in the original list\n    is preserved in the returned list.\n\n    Args:\n        strings (List[str]): A list of strings to filter.\n        prefix (str): The prefix string to match.\n\n    Returns:\n        List[str]: A new list containing strings from the input list that\n                   start with the specified prefix.\n\n    Examples:\n        >>> filter_by_prefix([], 'a')\n        []\n        >>> filter_by_prefix(['abc', 'bcd', 'cde', 'array'], 'a')\n        ['abc', 'array']\n        >>> filter_by_prefix(['Hello', 'hello', 'world'], 'H')\n        ['Hello']\n        >>> filter_by_prefix(['apple', 'banana'], 'z')\n        []\n    \"\"\"\n    result = []\n    for s in strings:\n        if s.startswith(prefix):\n            result.append(s)\n    return result\n```"}
