{"task_id": "HumanEval/60", "solution": "```python\ndef sum_to_n(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of all positive integers from 1 up to a given integer n.\n\n    If n is positive, it returns the sum 1 + 2 + ... + n.\n    If n is 0 or negative, it returns 0.\n\n    Args:\n        n: The input integer.\n\n    Returns:\n        The sum of integers from 1 to n, or 0 if n is not positive.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If the input 'n' is not an integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'n' must be an integer.\")\n\n    if n <= 0:\n        return 0\n    else:\n        # Use Gauss's summation formula for O(1) performance\n        return (n * (n + 1)) // 2\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/60", "solution": "```python\ndef sum_to_n(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of all integers from 1 up to a given integer n.\n\n    Args:\n        n: An integer representing the upper limit of the summation.\n           Must be a non-negative integer.\n\n    Returns:\n        The sum of integers from 1 to n. Returns 0 if n is 0.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If n is not an integer.\n        ValueError: If n is a negative integer.\n\n    Examples:\n        >>> sum_to_n(30)\n        465\n        >>> sum_to_n(100)\n        5050\n        >>> sum_to_n(5)\n        15\n        >>> sum_to_n(1)\n        1\n        >>> sum_to_n(0)\n        0\n        >>> sum_to_n(-1)\n        Traceback (most recent call last):\\\n            ...\\\n        ValueError: Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer for sum_to_n.\n        >>> sum_to_n(3.14)\n        Traceback (most recent call last):\\\n            ...\\\n        TypeError: Input 'n' must be an integer.\n        >>> sum_to_n(\"abc\")\n        Traceback (most recent call last):\\\n            ...\\\n        TypeError: Input 'n' must be an integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'n' must be an integer.\")\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer for sum_to_n.\")\n\n    return n * (n + 1) // 2\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/61", "solution": "```python\ndef correct_bracketing(brackets: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if a given string of parentheses is correctly bracketed.\n\n    A string is considered correctly bracketed if every opening bracket has a\n    corresponding closing bracket in the correct Last-In, First-Out (LIFO) order.\n\n    Args:\n        brackets: A string consisting solely of opening '(' and closing ')'\n                  bracket characters.\n\n    Returns:\n        True if the input 'brackets' string is correctly bracketed, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    balance = 0\n    for char in brackets:\n        if char == '(':\n            balance += 1\n        elif char == ')':\n            balance -= 1\n        \n        # If balance goes below zero, it means a closing bracket appeared\n        # without a corresponding open bracket.\n        if balance < 0:\n            return False\n            \n    # After iterating through the entire string, if balance is 0, all\n    # opening brackets have been matched.\n    return balance == 0\n```"}
