{"task_id": "HumanEval/62", "solution": "```python\ndef derivative(xs: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the derivative of a polynomial represented by a list of coefficients.\n\n    Args:\n        xs: A list of numerical coefficients (int or float). xs[i] corresponds\n            to the coefficient of x^i.\n\n    Returns:\n        A new list of numerical coefficients representing the derivative polynomial.\n        output[j] corresponds to the coefficient of x^j in the derivative.\n        The length of the output list will be max(0, len(xs) - 1).\n        If the input polynomial is a constant or empty, the output list will be empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    # 1. Handle Edge Cases:\n    # If the input list is empty (empty polynomial) or contains only one element\n    # (constant polynomial, e.g., [5] representing 5x^0),\n    # its derivative is zero, represented by an empty list.\n    if len(xs) <= 1:\n        return []\n\n    # 2. Initialize Result List:\n    result_coeffs = []\n\n    # 3. Iterate and Calculate Coefficients:\n    # Loop through the input coefficients starting from the second element (index 1).\n    # The term xs[0] (constant term) differentiates to zero and is not included.\n    # For a term xs[i] * x^i, its derivative is (xs[i] * i) * x^(i-1).\n    # So, the new coefficient (xs[i] * i) will be at index (i-1) in the result list.\n    for i in range(1, len(xs)):\n        coeff = xs[i]           # Original coefficient for x^i\n        power = i               # Original power of x\n\n        derived_coeff = coeff * power\n        result_coeffs.append(derived_coeff)\n\n    # 4. Return Result:\n    return result_coeffs\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/62", "solution": "```python\ndef derivative(xs: list) -> list:\n    n = len(xs)\n\n    # Handle edge cases for empty list or constant polynomial\n    # A polynomial of degree 0 (constant) has a derivative of 0,\n    # represented canonically by an empty list of coefficients.\n    # An empty input list also represents the zero polynomial,\n    # whose derivative is also the zero polynomial (empty list).\n    if n <= 1:\n        return []\n\n    derivative_coefficients = []\n    # Iterate from the second coefficient (index 1) to the end.\n    # xs[i] is the coefficient for x^i.\n    # The derivative of xs[i] * x^i is (i * xs[i]) * x^(i-1).\n    # The new coefficient (i * xs[i]) goes into the derivative list\n    # at the index corresponding to power (i-1).\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        # Calculate the new coefficient for x^(i-1)\n        new_coeff = i * xs[i]\n        derivative_coefficients.append(new_coeff)\n\n    return derivative_coefficients\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/63", "solution": "```python\ndef fibfib(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the n-th element of the FibFib number sequence.\n\n    The FibFib sequence is defined as:\n    fibfib(0) == 0\n    fibfib(1) == 0\n    fibfib(2) == 1\n    fibfib(n) == fibfib(n-1) + fibfib(n-2) + fibfib(n-3) for n > 2.\n\n    Args:\n        n: An integer representing the index in the FibFib sequence.\n           Must be a non-negative integer.\n\n    Returns:\n        The n-th FibFib number.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If 'n' is not an integer.\n        ValueError: If 'n' is a negative integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    # FR-FF-003: Input Validation - Check type\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'n' must be an integer.\")\n\n    # FR-FF-003: Input Validation - Check non-negativity\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    # FR-FF-001: Base Cases Computation\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 0\n    if n == 2:\n        return 1\n\n    # Initialize DP table (list) to store computed FibFib numbers\n    # Size n+1 to access up to index n\n    # PR-FF-002: O(n) space complexity\n    dp_table = [0] * (n + 1)\n\n    # Set initial base cases in the DP table\n    dp_table[0] = 0\n    dp_table[1] = 0\n    dp_table[2] = 1\n\n    # FR-FF-002: Recursive Case Computation using tabulation (bottom-up DP)\n    # PR-FF-001: O(n) time complexity\n    for i in range(3, n + 1):\n        dp_table[i] = dp_table[i - 1] + dp_table[i - 2] + dp_table[i - 3]\n\n    # Return the n-th FibFib number from the table\n    return dp_table[n]\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/63", "solution": "```python\ndef fibfib(n: int) -> int:\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 0\n    if n == 2:\n        return 1\n\n    # Initialize a, b, c to represent fibfib(0), fibfib(1), fibfib(2) respectively.\n    # These will be shifted to represent fibfib(k-3), fibfib(k-2), fibfib(k-1)\n    # as the loop progresses.\n    a = 0  # Corresponds to fibfib(i-3) initially fibfib(0)\n    b = 0  # Corresponds to fibfib(i-2) initially fibfib(1)\n    c = 1  # Corresponds to fibfib(i-1) initially fibfib(2)\n\n    # Iterate from i = 3 up to n to compute fibfib(n)\n    for _ in range(3, n + 1):\n        next_fib = a + b + c\n        a = b\n        b = c\n        c = next_fib\n\n    return c\n```"}
